A||||45||william_thorniii||Seat Covers?||||5||
Z||000000||william_thorniii||01-06-2000||04:45 PM||||Ladies and Gentlemen,<P>First I am not a fan of leather seats.  So with that out of the way... Does anybody have a nice set of seat covers on their Fiero?  I know that IRM and the Fiero Store sell covers, has anybody tried them?  If so were you happy?  If I cannot find something suitable, I will buy racing seats.  If that pans out any suggestions on a set of seats in the $400 range?<P>Many Thanks,<P>William T. Thorn, III<P>By the way, I have researched old threads and am not interested in the Duct Tape Covers... ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Shiner||01-06-2000||04:55 PM||||I am not a huge fan of leather seats either.  I am going to need to replace the seat covers when I restore my GT.  I WAS going to go with Mr Mikes leather though.  I think that leather would solve the rubbing on the side bolster wear problem though.  And at almost $300 for fiero store GT seat covers, it makes sense to go Mr. Mikes.  I would like to hear feedback on the cloth seats as well, and also feedback from people who have done Mr. Mikes covers.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||01-06-2000||05:45 PM||||I have seen one car with Mr. Mikes covers on and it looks very good.  I won't divulge his name since he's on the forum but he'll know who I'm talking about if he reads this.  I took some pics of his car but didn't think to take any of the interior.  <P>That said, I prefer a cloth seat, but I'm not going to spend the same amount of money for cloth that I would for leather!  I went to an upolsterer (I spelled that wrong, didn't I?) and he want to charge almost $500 for new cloth seat cover! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Sorry, but for $100 less I'll take leather from Mr. Mikes.  BTW-The only reason I don't want leather is because it tends to be hot in the summer and cold in the winter, otherwise I'd take it in a heartbeat.||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||01-06-2000||06:31 PM||||That is the similar to what I have found.  In fact to reinstall an original seat cover, I was told that a conservative estimate would be $125.  No Thanks.  <P>Hey SCCA guys, what do you use?  I would like to go with a 4 pt. harnass and racing seats.  I like the style of the Corbeau Targa, are there any other seats similar for less $?  Mind you that this is for driving as well as racing and that is why I want a seat with some padding.  Any suggestions?<P>Anyone...<P>Bueller...<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
Z||000004||Richard Parnell||01-06-2000||08:35 PM||||I put in a set of seat covers that are made of the same material as wet suits.  They're a local Hawaii product that came out cause guys didn't want seat covers that soak up water after getting out of the ocean after surfing or diving.  They look pretty sharp but took a while to mold down into the seat contours. They cost about $100 a couple of years ago.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||01-06-2000||08:41 PM||||Hey... Those would be great for people with leaking t-tops and sun roofs too!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Seriously, that material should hold up a lot better than the factory stuff. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||william_thorniii||01-06-2000||08:50 PM||||Now that's a good idea!<P>I could get used to that... anybody know where/if they are available on-line.  Ultimately I would like covers that could have some royal blue accents to match the rest of the car.. My fiancee has already named this progect the "Smurf-Mobile".  I guess she doesn't like my use of royal blue.  Perhaps I will paint the exterior a color more drab.. I digress... <BR>I just saw Kilkey seats on Summit's web-page has anyone seen/tried any of these.  The prices are better than RCI and are therefore VERY affordable.  I only wonder if they would be comfortable enough for a driver.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000007||Richard Parnell||01-06-2000||08:54 PM||||If you'd like I'll contact the company and see if they're online.  I'll post any info I find for everyone.  I know they make them custom too 'cause my son got some made for his rice burner and they look sharp.||||reg||6
Z||000008||william_thorniii||01-06-2000||09:07 PM||||Richard, <P>I would REALLY appreciate that.  Earlier you said that they took about a month before they "fit" the seat, does that mean that they look like they were made for the seat now?  Also, do they cover the back too?  I realize that those are minor concerns, but I am curious.<P>Thanks Again,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000009||Dave85||01-06-2000||09:09 PM||||Richard,<BR>I would be interested in a set of those! Any info would be great.<P>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000010||Richard Parnell||01-06-2000||09:20 PM||||Guys-  I called the company (Wet Okole, which is wet butt in local jargon) and got their web address.   <A HREF="http://www.wetokole.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.wetokole.com</A> <BR>I checked the site out and man I think I'm gonna get a new set for my car.  They have so many more colors than when I bought my set.  I don't think you'll have to woryy about the fit.  Mine were just a generic set they made when they first came out but the new ones like on my son's car fit like they were factory installed.  Check the site out, I think you'll be pleasantly surprised.||||reg||6
Z||000011||Richard Parnell||01-06-2000||09:30 PM||||I noticed that they have a section on their web site with pictures of different cars they've done and it looks like you can get logos on the seat covers.  I'm definately going to have them make me a new set for my car with the Fiero logo on them.  I'll see if they'll put my Fieros' interior on their samples site.||||reg||6
Z||000012||william_thorniii||01-06-2000||09:35 PM||||Richard,<P>Thanks!  I already ordered color swatches.  This Forum really pays off!  If there are any other suggestions out there lets keep them coming.  Although these look promising... I haven't given them my VISA yet.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
