Z||000041||william_thorniii||01-12-2000||08:49 PM||||Richard,<P>Thanks for the input about the heat.  I am sure that I wouldn't go as far as the beads and a seat cover.  It is not that they would look too hoky.... er... I mean they would look too hoky, but that isn't the reason that I would not put them on my car.  Springs, foam, upholstery, seat cover and beads would simply be too much.  I would need to lean the seat back to refrain from hitting my head on the roof.  <P>I have taken the liberty of contacting Mr. Mikes about this dilema.  We are far from a definite answer though.  I think that I am going to hold out for a while though and see if anything surfaces. <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
