Z||000044||william_thorniii||01-13-2000||07:26 PM||||Phil,<P>I called several upholstery shops locally and nationally.  One particular conversation was regarding them only re-stitching factory original covers and installing them.  They estimated the seats to run $150.  Remember that does not even include the fabric or much of the labor since it would be pre-cut.  As much as I would enjoy giving my $ to a local business it is not prudent.  <P>William T. Thorn, III ||||reg||1
Z||000046||Phil||01-13-2000||07:43 PM||||Oh! I suppose new seat covers would be a real "asset" ||||reg||1
